ize-967849.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[An Illinois thrift store has collected more than 100,000 donated items and runs with 200 volunteers]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134416126.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[House of Hope Resale, located in Barrington, Illinois, serves as a vital resource for families in financial distress. The non-profit efficiently manages more than 100,000 donated items, supported by a dedicated team of 200 volunteers. Sales revenue from the store is fully utilized for emergency assistance, providing crucial support for rent, utilities, and medical bills. Community engagement is fostered through events and digital platforms to recruit more volunteers.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-illinois-thrift-store-has-collected-more-than-100000-donated-items-and-runs-with-200-regular-volunteers-using-every-resale-purchase-to-support-local-families-in-crisis/articleshow/134416126.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-illinois-thrift-store-has-collected-more-than-100000-donated-items-and-runs-with-200-regular-volunteers-using-every-resale-purchase-to-support-local-families-in-crisis/articleshow/134416126.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-22T22:10:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134416711,imgsize-1332397.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[From tariff overlord to tarmac man, Trump to roll out red carpet for Xi]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134415950.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/from-tariff-overlord-to-tarmac-man-donald-trump-to-roll-ou