:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134412832,imgsize-1864148.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[From law school to selling 1 million bags of firewood]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134413035.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-the-1980s-an-australian-man-left-law-school-to-run-his-family-farm-after-his-father-died-when-drought-and-bushfires-devastated-his-670-hectare-property-he-began-selling-fallen-firewood-door-to-door-now-his-business-sells-1-million-bags-a-year/articleshow/134413035.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-the-1980s-an-australian-man-left-law-school-to-run-his-family-farm-after-his-father-died-when-drought-and-bushfires-devastated-his-670-hectare-property-he-began-selling-fallen-firewood-door-to-door-now-his-business-sells-1-million-bags-a-year/articleshow/134413035.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-22T18:35:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134413163,imgsize-338145.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Sanat Pandit: Ann Arbor sixth-grader’s $300 drone extinguished 18 of 20 test fires]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134411967.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A sixth-grader from Ann Arbor, Michigan, has developed a low-cost firefighting drone designed to help tackle one of the most dangerous challenges faced by firefighters: reaching and suppressing fires without putting people directly in harm’s way. Sanat Pandit, a student at Greenhills School, built a $300 unmanned aerial vehicle that uses thermal imaging, sonar and path-planning technology to locate and target hot spots.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/meet-sanat-pandit-the-ann-arbor-sixth-grader-whose-300-firefighting-drone-extinguished-18-of-20-outdoor-test-fires-and-earned-him-a-national-stem-final-spot/articleshow/134411967.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/meet-sanat-pandit-the-ann-arbor-sixth-grader-whose-300-firefighting-drone-extinguished-18-of-20-outdoor-test-fires-and-earned-him-a-national-stem-final-spot/articleshow/134411967.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-22T19:17:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134412145,imgsize-1730988.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[From being fired at her job at 27 to building an $800 million luxury brand: The Tamara Mellon Story]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134411151.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[At 27, Tamara Mellon was fired from British Vogue, struggling with drug addiction and living in her parents’ basement. A year later, she co-founded Jimmy Choo with shoemaker Jimmy Choo, borrowing £150,000 from her father to build the business. Her fashion instincts, celebrity strategy and business drive helped turn the small London operation into a global luxury footwear brand.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/from-being-fired-at-her-job-at-27-to-building-an-800-million-luxury-brand-how-tamara-mellon-turned-a-career-crisis-into-a-fashion-empire/articleshow/134411151.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/from-being-fired-at-her-job-at-27-to-building-an-800-million-luxury-brand-how-tamara-mellon-turned-a-career-crisis-into-a-fashion-empire/articleshow/134411151.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-22T17:50:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134411564,imgsize-844246.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['I'm going to tell the truth': Netanyahu hits back at Mamdani ahead of UN speech]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134413385.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu is set to deliver a significant address at the United Nations General Assembly. In his speech, he intends to staunchly defend military operations conducted by Israel while also targeting New York City Mayor Zohran Mamdani. Netanyahu has accused Mamdani of endorsing Hamas and fostering anti-Jewish sentiment, in response to Mamdani's previous remarks labeling him a war criminal responsible for genocide.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/im-going-to-tell-the-truth-netanyahu-hits-back-at-mamdani-ahead-of-un-speech/articleshow/134413385.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/im-going-to-tell-the-truth-netanyahu-hits-back-at-mamdani-ahead-of-un-speech/articleshow/134413385.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-22T18:48:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134413518,imgsize-1351844.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Putin, Saudi crown prince discuss safe passage through Hormuz, Bab el-Mandeb]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134413185.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/putin-saudi-crown-prince-discuss-safe-pas